  "domain": "machine-learning",
  "definition": "An Implicit Neural Representation (INR) is a method of encoding continuous signals\u2014such as 3D shapes, scenes, or images\u2014as the weights of a neural network rather than as discrete grids or meshes. The network acts as a function that maps spatial or temporal coordinates to signal values, enabling theoretically infinite resolution. INRs are widely used in novel-view synthesis, shape reconstruction, and physics simulation.",
